## Feature #7 Increment 2 (spec §4.7 Correction 1) — the virtual clock covers
## SYNC `Instant` time too, not just the async sleep deadline. `Instant.now` /
## `Instant.elapsed` sample the monotonic clock INDEPENDENTLY of
## `ruxen_time_now_ns` (the async-sleep seam), so they must ALSO route through
## the TestClock seam to be virtual in a test — which they do.
##
## With the clock installed: take an `Instant`, `advance` virtual time by 5
## minutes, then `elapsed()` reports EXACTLY the virtual delta (300s = 300000ms),
## NOT the real wall-clock (which is ~0ms — the test runs in milliseconds). So a
## test of time-based logic measured with `Instant` sees deterministic virtual
## time. (Without the Correction-1 fix, `elapsed()` would read the real clock
## and report ~0, since no real time passed.)

use std.time.Instant
use std.time.Duration

def main
  puts "instant start"
  var guard = TestClock.install
  let start = Instant.now()
  # Advance 5 virtual minutes. No real time passes.
  TestClock.advance(Duration.from_secs(300))
  let elapsed = start.elapsed()
  let ms = elapsed.as_millis()
  puts "elapsed_ms=#{ms}"
  puts "instant done"
end
